{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RSZIsoformalInterface","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.GlobalBirkhoffSuppliesAmplitude.gives_lift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.GlobalBirkhoffSuppliesAmplitude.gives_lift","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesAmplitudeE.lean#L222-L222","doc":"and it drives the even-face correction to the physical lift `κ > 1` (unreachable by the\nself-adjoint branching Schur complement, `A3OffBlockDerivation.magnitudeFactor_le_one`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.GlobalBirkhoffSuppliesAmplitude.birkhoff_pins","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.GlobalBirkhoffSuppliesAmplitude.birkhoff_pins","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesAmplitudeE.lean#L219-L219","doc":"The amplitude `E` — pinned by the GLOBAL Birkhoff connection matrix, not any local\nStokes constant — breaks graded self-adjointness (`E ≠ 0`; forced by the strict lift\nvia `amplitude_nonzero`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.GlobalBirkhoffSuppliesAmplitude.multislope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.GlobalBirkhoffSuppliesAmplitude.multislope","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesAmplitudeE.lean#L215-L215","doc":"The carrier module has ≥ 2 distinct Newton slopes: its local isoformal moduli is\nnonempty (`1 ≤ dim`).  Necessary for any local Stokes freedom\n(`local_stokes_lift_forces_positive_dim`); it is precisely what C1's pure-isoclinic\n`∞` (`rszIsoformalDim_one = 0`) fails to have. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.GlobalBirkhoffSuppliesAmplitude.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.GlobalBirkhoffSuppliesAmplitude.mk","kind":"ctor","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesAmplitudeE.lean#L209-L209","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.GlobalBirkhoffSuppliesAmplitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.GlobalBirkhoffSuppliesAmplitude","kind":"class","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesAmplitudeE.lean#L188-L222","doc":"**§3b dependent conjecture — the amplitude `E` is supplied by the GLOBAL Birkhoff\nconnection matrix, not by local Stokes data.**\n\n`@conjecture: dependent` (its content depends on the open construction of the global\n`0↔∞` q-monodromy / Birkhoff connection matrix of the carrier module — theta-valued,\nun-started; #4790's successor W2 and\n`docs/audits/2026-08-01-branch-selection-birkhoff-connection-matrix.md`).\n\nDistinct from `A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.DerivedAmplitudeGivesLift` (which names the DM\nq-cubic prolongation symbol): this carrier records the WALL's positive branch — a\n**multi-slope** carrier whose local Stokes moduli is nonempty (necessary, by\n`local_stokes_lift_forces_positive_dim`), with the amplitude pinned by the **global**\nBirkhoff datum rather than any local Stokes constant.\n\n**Content-bearing, not self-assuming.**  `multislope` carries the RSZ necessary\ncondition (`1 ≤ dim`, an INPUT the geometry must satisfy); `birkhoff_pins` is the forced\n`E ≠ 0` (tied to the lift by `amplitude_nonzero`); `gives_lift` carries the physical\nlift as a hypothesis.  **No instance is supplied**: building the theta-valued Birkhoff\nmatrix and reading `E` off it is the open successor; discharging this by *choosing* `E`\nto hit `κ` (`stokesAmplitude_surjective_of_dim_pos` / `amplitude_surjective`) is the\nforbidden fit and is not done. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.stokesAmplitude_surjective_of_dim_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.stokesAmplitude_surjective_of_dim_pos","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesAmplitudeE.lean#L173-L184","doc":"**Positive isoformal dimension ⇒ the local amplitude is SURJECTIVE onto `R` (sorry-free).**\nWhen `d ≥ 1` the coordinate sum reaches every target (fix `coeff ≡ 1`, put the target on\none coordinate).  So a nonempty local Stokes moduli leaves the amplitude `E` **entirely\nfree**: local Stokes data does not select its value.  Mirrors\n`A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.amplitude_surjective` at the moduli level — the value of `E` must\ncome from the GLOBAL (`0↔∞`) Birkhoff connection matrix, not from local Stokes data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.local_stokes_lift_forces_positive_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.local_stokes_lift_forces_positive_dim","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesAmplitudeE.lean#L158-L169","doc":"**A local-Stokes lift forces positive isoformal dimension (sorry-free).**  Contrapositive\nof Part 2: if the local-Stokes amplitude produces a genuine lift `> 1`, the moduli\ndimension is `≥ 1`, i.e. the carrier module has ≥ 2 distinct Newton slopes.  A pure\nisoclinic carrier (like C1's `∞`) is thereby excluded as the source of the lift. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.pureIsoclinic_local_stokes_cannot_lift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.pureIsoclinic_local_stokes_cannot_lift","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesAmplitudeE.lean#L137-L154","doc":"**A single-slope module's local Stokes data cannot produce the A=3 lift (sorry-free).**\nComposing Part 1 with `A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.amplitude_nonzero` (a genuine lift forces\n`E ≠ 0`): if the local-Stokes amplitude is drawn from a zero-dimensional isoformal\nmoduli (`d = 0`, pure isoclinic), it equals `0`, so the even-face correction stays at\nthe self-adjoint value `≤ 1` — **no lift**.\n\n**Scope-(b) structural exclusion**, cited invariant = the emptiness of the RSZ\nslope-pairing index set at `k = 1` (`rszIsoformalDim_one`, a proved dimension bound).\nWhat is excluded is *the local Stokes datum of a single-slope carrier as a source of the\nlift* — not resurgence's role in the magnitude generally, and not the ±i discontinuity's\nexistence (proved elsewhere). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.c1_isoformal_toNat_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.c1_isoformal_toNat_zero","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesAmplitudeE.lean#L127-L133","doc":"**C1's `∞` supplies zero local moduli (sorry-free).**  The pure-isoclinic single edge\n`(r, d) = (2, 1)` at C1's `∞` (after the forced ramified pullback, `k = 1`) has\nisoformal dimension `0` (`rszIsoformalDim_one`), so `(rszIsoformalDim 1 r μ).toNat = 0`.\nThis is the RSZ input that places C1 in the vanishing branch of Part 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.stokesAmplitude_eq_zero_of_dim_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.stokesAmplitude_eq_zero_of_dim_zero","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesAmplitudeE.lean#L116-L125","doc":"**Zero isoformal moduli ⇒ zero local Stokes amplitude (sorry-free).**  With no\nslope-pairing coordinates (`d = 0`) the coordinate sum is empty, hence `0`.  This is the\namplitude-level content of RSZ `rszIsoformalDim_one` / #4790's\n`c1_infinity_isoformalDim_eq_zero`: a pure isoclinic module has no local Stokes data to\nBE the amplitude. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.stokesAmplitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesAmplitudeE.stokesAmplitude","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesAmplitudeE.lean#L103-L112","doc":"**The amplitude a LOCAL q-Stokes datum can supply**, as the coordinate sum of the\nstrictly-off-block nilpotent part `N` of the unipotent q-Stokes matrix `St = I + N`\nover the `d` slope-pairing moduli (RSZ Thm 3.3.5 supplies `d = rszIsoformalDim`; Thm\n5.5.7 supplies the unipotency ⇒ **no constant term**).\n\nA linear form with zero constant term: the vanishing at `d = 0` below is the faithful\nRSZ statement that a single-slope module has no strictly-off-block part, NOT a smuggled\ndecomposition of `E`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}